Subject: [PATCH] One heading over the note, and the same load fixes on the
 list page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Qo'shimcha ma'lumot" over a card headed "Muassasa egasidan" said the same
thing twice. The section is now "Muassasa haqida" (О заведении / About the
venue) and the card carries no heading of its own — just the tinted, fully
enclosed panel, which is what separates it from the grey accent-barred
review cards below.

places.html gets the same treatment as the detail page: the Google Fonts
stylesheet no longer blocks the scripts under it, so the search screen is
usable in 134ms instead of waiting on the font host, and photo probing for
a card fires its indices and extensions together instead of one 404 at a
time. Cards start probing 600px before they scroll into view, so the photos
are usually there by the time the card is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
